1. Berkeley Function Calling Leaderboard — official checkers (vendored code)
================================================================================

Location:  src/mini_thalamus/evals/external/bfcl_official/

Source:    BFCL, part of the Gorilla project (UC Berkeley)
           https://github.com/ShishirPatil/gorilla
           https://gorilla.cs.berkeley.edu/leaderboard.html
           Obtained from the `bfcl-eval` distribution on PyPI.

License:   Apache License 2.0
           http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Modifications: the vendored subtree was renamed on import from `bfcl_eval` to
`bfcl_official_impl` so it cannot collide with an installed `bfcl-eval`
package, and only the multi-turn evaluator subset needed by this project's
harness was taken. The scoring logic itself is unmodified. The subset and the
rename are scripted in mini_thalamus/evals/vendor_bfcl_multi_turn.py, which
takes the wheel to vendor from as an argument; the exact upstream version used
is not recorded in this repository.

A copy of the Apache License 2.0 is available at the URL above. Where the
Apache License requires that a NOTICE file be carried forward, this file
serves that purpose.


